// Symbols plugin — type a name, get the glyph.
//
// A REAL PREFIX, and that matters for two reasons.
//
// 1. With no prefix (""), the plugin treats every keystroke as a match against
//    every symbol name. An empty query then fuzzy-matches the entire table, so
//    opening the runner produced a wall of junk rows — "SPACE", "!",
//    "QUOTATION MARK" — that outranked real results and filled the list. That
//    is exactly the startup behaviour this prefix removes.
// 2. It keeps symbols out of the way of normal searching. Nobody types a symbol
//    name by accident looking for an app.
//
// ";" is the prefix: `;arrow` offers → ↑ ← ↓. Rarely typed in a launcher query,
// so it will not collide with an application name.
//
// This exists because the machine already depends on Nerd Font glyphs for waybar
// and kitty; pasting one used to mean looking it up elsewhere.

Config(
    prefix: ";",
    max_entries: 8,
)
